---
import PartHead from "../coverage/PartHead.astro";
import NextPart from "../coverage/NextPart.astro";
import Check from "../lesson/Check.astro";
import Choice from "../lesson/Choice.astro";
import AiCard from "./AiCard.astro";
import { rewind, story, tableB } from "../../lib/archive";
import { spell } from "../../lib/cases";

const ask = "Can you rebuild Friday's table from the pages you kept, without asking a single site again, and show me you did?";
const down = rewind.unavailable.map((u) => u.name).join(" and ");
const criteria = [
  `Replay the schedule pages Friday's capture manifest lists: the ${spell(rewind.schedulesSaved)} it saved, each matched to its content hash, and ${down} listed as unavailable, not left out.`,
  "Make zero network requests, counted by a counter you show catching a test request.",
  "Name the fingerprint of the fixed parser and the revision of the code that built the table.",
  "Diff Tuesday's table against the rebuild, and explain every changed cell.",
];

const find = (test: (l: string) => boolean, what: string) => rewind.lines.find(test) ?? (() => { throw new Error(`the replay report has no ${what} line`); })();
const tidy = (l: string) => l.trim().replace(/\s+:\s/, ": ").replace(/\s{2,}/g, " ");
const claims: [string, string][] = [
  ["bytes", "These are Friday's pages, byte for byte"],
  ["dropped", "No site was quietly dropped"],
  ["asked", "No site was asked"],
  ["code", "The fixed parser produced this table"],
  ["cause", "Only the name changed, and the tidy rule changed it"],
];
const claimText = Object.fromEntries(claims);
const lines = [
  { text: find((l) => l.startsWith("replayed "), "replayed"), answer: "bytes", why: "Each page matched the hash Friday's manifest recorded. Without that, these could be any copies of the pages." },
  { text: find((l) => l.startsWith("listed "), "listed"), answer: "dropped", why: `Without it, nothing shows the rebuild accounted for ${down}, whose page was never saved.` },
  { text: find((l) => l.startsWith("requests "), "requests"), answer: "asked", why: "Without it, nothing measured the network at all." },
  { text: find((l) => l.startsWith("fingerprint "), "fingerprint"), answer: "code", why: "Without it, the table could have come from Tuesday's parser or any other version." },
  { text: find((l) => /^\s+\S.*->/.test(l) && l.includes(story.fixedName), "changed cell"), answer: "cause", why: "Without it, “1 cell changed” says how many, not which one or why." },
].map((l) => ({ ...l, text: tidy(l.text), why: `${claimText[l.answer]}. ${l.why}` }));

const draft: [string, string][] = [
  ["reads", `It should count the ${rewind.schedulesSaved} page reads, since reading a saved page is a request.`],
  ["counter", "Nothing shows the counter would have noticed a request, so its 0 proves nothing."],
  ["fingerprint", "The fingerprint already shows nothing was fetched, so the line is redundant."],
  ["offline", "A replay can't make requests at all, so the line belongs nowhere in the report."],
];
---

<section id="rewind" class="ar-part">
  <PartHead id="rewind">Rewind: Tuesday with a replay requirement</PartHead>
  <p>In Module 1's Rewind, one added sentence gave Kick <strong>acceptance criteria</strong>: conditions its work had to meet before Riley would accept it. Tuesday's question asks for the right thing. It doesn't yet say what evidence Riley will accept.</p>
  <p>The rebuild target is Monday's table, the one readers have, with one name fixed: {tableB.caption}, the same named gaps, and “{story.fixedName}” where Tuesday's table says “{story.tuesdayName}”.</p>
  <div class="cv-user-prompt" role="region" aria-label="Riley's question on Tuesday">
    <div class="cv-chat-bar">
      <span class="cv-chat-badge">Prompt</span>
      <span class="cv-chat-meta">Riley → Kick, Tuesday</span>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-chat-text">{ask}</p>
  </div>

  <div class="cv-commit ar-commit" data-commit>
    <p class="cv-kind">Write it <span>you check your own</span></p>
    <label class="cv-write" for="ar-criterion">Write one acceptance criterion that would let Riley check the rebuild instead of taking Kick's word for it.</label>
    <textarea id="ar-criterion" rows="2" placeholder="Done means the report shows..." data-save="rewind-criterion"></textarea>
    <div class="cv-actions">
      <button type="button" data-commit-btn disabled>Compare with Riley's</button>
      <button type="button" class="cv-link-btn" data-commit-skip>Skip and show Riley's</button>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-once" data-needs-note>Write a short sentence to compare, or skip ahead.</p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <div class="cv-user-prompt" role="region" aria-label="Riley's question with acceptance criteria">
        <div class="cv-chat-bar">
          <span class="cv-chat-badge">Prompt</span>
          <span class="cv-chat-meta">Riley → Kick, with acceptance criteria</span>
        </div>
        <p class="cv-chat-text">{ask} Done means your report shows all four:</p>
        <ol class="ar-criteria">{criteria.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}</ol>
      </div>
      <fieldset class="cv-ticks">
        <legend>Check what yours covers:</legend>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="rewind-has-inputs" /><span>Pins the inputs: Friday's pages, identified by content hash, with the missing one named</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="rewind-has-counter" /><span>Makes “no requests” a measurement, not a promise</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="rewind-has-code" /><span>Identifies the code that produced the table</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-save="rewind-has-diff" /><span>Requires every change in the table to be explained</span></label>
      </fieldset>
      <p>Each criterion asks for evidence that could have come out differently: a hash can fail to match, a counter can count, a diff can show a cell nobody explained. Evidence that could never fail proves nothing.</p>

      <h3>Kick's replay report</h3>
      <p class="cv-label">Real lab output from <code>python labs/m02_archive.py</code>, quoted whole. The build checks it against the sample and the lab.</p>
      <div class="cv-agent-reply ar-reply" role="region" aria-label="Kick's replay report">
        <div class="cv-chat-bar">
          <span class="cv-agent-badge">Kick · Coding agent</span>
          <span class="cv-status-ok">{rewind.requests} requests · {rewind.cellsChanged} cell changed</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="ar-report" tabindex="0" aria-label="Replay report"><code>{rewind.lines.join("\n")}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p>Two lines identify the code. The <strong>fingerprint</strong>, {rewind.fingerprint}, is Case 3's hash of the parser module, its page reader and its config. The <strong>build revision</strong>, {rewind.buildRevision}, is the git blob hash of the program that built the table, so it changes whenever that file does. Neither can be turned back into code. Anyone with the repository can hash their copy and compare, and with the pages Friday's manifest names, the same code gives the same table.</p>

      <h4 class="cv-try">Check the report against the criteria</h4>
      <Check once="rewind-match" kind="Apply it" note="Answer all six, then check.">
        <p class="cv-qlabel">Cut each line below from the report. Which claim could Riley no longer check?</p>
        {lines.map((l, i) => (
          <div class="cv-line ar-match" data-q data-type="select" data-answer={l.answer} data-why={l.why}>
            <label class="cv-stack"><code>{l.text}</code>
              <select data-save={`rewind-cut-${i}`} aria-label={`Claim that depends on the line ${l.text}`}><option value="">Choose a claim</option>{claims.map(([v, t]) => <option value={v}>{t}</option>)}</select>
            </label>
            <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
          </div>
        ))}
        <Choice radio save="rewind-draft" label={`Kick's first draft said only “requests: ${rewind.requests}”. Riley sent it back. Why?`}
          options={draft} answer="counter"
          why="A counter nobody has seen catch anything reads 0 both when nothing was fetched and when it misses connections. The finished line says it caught a name lookup and a direct connection first, so its 0 is a measurement."
          wrong={{ reads: "A replay reads saved pages from disk. A request goes over the network, and the point is that there were none.", fingerprint: "The fingerprint names the code. A re-fetch with the fixed parser has the same fingerprint, so it says nothing about the network.", offline: "Kick's own plan was to re-fetch. Nothing stops code from making requests during a rebuild, so the report has to measure it." }} />
        <p slot="reveal">Every claim in the report rests on a line that could have come out differently, and each line answers one of Riley's criteria. Without the criteria, the same report is a page of text you either trust or don't. With them, Riley can check it in a minute, and so can anyone Riley sends the table to.</p>
      </Check>
    </div>
  </div>
  <AiCard part="rewind" />
  <NextPart from="rewind">This bug was caught in a day. What if one stays hidden for months?</NextPart>
</section>

<style>
  .ar-part :global(fieldset.cv-line > label) { display: flex; flex-wrap: nowrap; align-items: flex-start; margin-right: 0; }
  .ar-part :global(fieldset.cv-line > label > span) { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; }
  .ar-part :global(fieldset.cv-line > label > input) { flex: none; margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .ar-part :global(.cv-chat-bar) { flex-wrap: wrap; row-gap: 0.35rem; }
  .ar-commit { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .ar-criteria { margin: -0.4rem 0 0; padding: 0 1.1rem 0.9rem 2.6rem; color: var(--sl-color-white); }
  .ar-criteria li { margin: 0.3rem 0; }
  .ar-report { margin: 0; padding: 0.85rem 1rem; border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: var(--tl-bg); font-size: 0.74rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .ar-report code { padding: 0; background: none; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .ar-match code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .ar-match { padding: 0.5rem 0 0.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--tl-line); }
</style>
